-- title:
--   Genuine original stopped Gaussian, small-jump, large-jump martingales with zero-clock source cancellation
-- statement:
--   Construct original stopped Gaussian, small-jump and large-jump compensated martingale terms, each with integrability, zero mean and exactly zero contribution whenever the natural bounded stopping clock is zero. Construct integrable nonpositive HJB-generator drift and dividend remainder and prove their original pathwise sum controls actual discounted terminal reserve and full closed dividend cash. The published theorem enables separate Gaussian, small-jump, large-jump and finite-variation agents to work concurrently.
-- source:
--   Direct original Ito-Meyer decomposition of the canonical fdb9a6a3 source type, strengthened by zero-stopping-clock component cancellation. Inputs may reuse original finite-grid L2 isometry, stopped Brownian/Gaussian bracket, Levy compensation, and Stieltjes cash accounting. Neither allcap positive expected budget nor descendant fdb0 residual is imported.

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AvramDividend_Classical_SpectrallyNegativeLevy
import Definitions.Def_AvramDividend_Classical_DividendStrategy

open MeasureTheory Set AvramDividend.Classical
